rlm-gar-rm [-n|--dry-run]

Delete Artifact Registry <repo>/<package> entries picked in an fzf
picker. TAB multi-selects; every selected package is confirmed
individually before anything is destroyed.

The package list, its cache, and the MRU history are shared with
gar-open — both commands read and refresh the same files under
~/.cache/gar-open/, so a refresh in either benefits the other.
Selecting --- REFRESH CACHE --- opens a secondary picker where you
TAB-multi-select which projects to re-fetch; entries for un-picked
projects are preserved.

The preview pane is deletion-oriented rather than browse-oriented
(that is gar-open's job): it reports the version count, total size on
disk, newest and oldest version timestamps, tag count, package
create/update time and annotations, the number of 1000-version delete
batches required, and a sample of the newest tagged versions. If the
version count cannot be determined — expired credentials, missing IAM
permission — the preview says so loudly instead of rendering an empty
package, because "no versions" reads as "safe to delete".

DELETION

Deletion runs in two phases per package, because
`gcloud artifacts packages delete` fails server-side on packages
holding more than 1000 versions:

  1. Versions are deleted in batches of at most 1000 via
     `gcloud artifacts versions delete --delete-tags`, re-counting
     between batches and continuing until none remain.
  2. The now-empty package is removed with
     `gcloud artifacts packages delete`.

Before the confirmation prompt, the exact gcloud command lines that
will run are printed, one argument per line. Digest lists are shown as
`<N version digest(s)>` rather than expanded — printing 1000 sha256
digests would bury the flags that determine what is destroyed. For
packages needing more than two batches, the first two are shown
followed by a note that the remaining batches are identical.

You confirm once per package; batches then proceed without further
prompting. After the batches finish, the package is re-queried to
verify it is really gone. If versions remain, the count is reported
and you are offered a retry. A batch that reports success without
reducing the version count aborts that package rather than looping.

Packages successfully deleted are pruned from the shared cache and the
MRU history so the next picker does not offer them.

OPTIONS
  -n, --dry-run
              Show the preview, the version counts, and the exact
              commands for every selected package, but run no deletes
              and ask no confirmations.

  -h, --help  Print usage and exit.

ENVIRONMENT
  GAR_SEARCH_PROJECTS
              Colon-separated list of GCP project IDs to browse.
              Required; the function errors out if not set. Shared
              with gar-open and gar-search.

REQUIRES
  gcloud, fzf, jq, curl, python3.

SEE ALSO
  gar-open    Browse the same package list and open a package in the
              Artifact Registry console.
  gar-search  Non-interactive substring search over the same packages.

NOTE
  OSC 8 hyperlinks in the preview pane require a terminal emulator
  that supports them (Kitty, Ghostty, iTerm2, WezTerm). Inside tmux
  also set: set -ga terminal-features "*:hyperlinks"
